From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 02:10:55 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 22/43] cef: treat the AROS RAM download path as safe

AROS provides RAM: as the default download directory and has no Linux desktop/home danger relationship. Avoid querying DIR_USER_DESKTOP, which canonicalizes a POSIX dot path and fatals during CEF initialization.

AI_PHASE: CEF_NATIVE_LIFECYCLE

AI_STATUS: aros-download-safety-fix-under-validation

AI_VALIDATION: cef_execute_process passed; cef_initialize symbolic stack ends at DownloadPathIsDangerous after stat('.') EINVAL and resource_util.cc DCHECK

AI_ASSUMPTION: RAM: is the deliberate volatile safe download target on AROS

AI_LIMITATIONS: CEF archive rebuild, resident relink, and initialization retry remain pending

AI_EVIDENCE: aros-opal-hosted-clean/test-artifacts/-cef-lifecycle-runtime-cmodel-fix-20260725/02-runtime.log

AI_DECISION_CHAIN:
---
 libcef/common/resource_util.cc | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libcef/common/resource_util.cc b/libcef/common/resource_util.cc
index e1b8ac90..6062804f 100644
--- a/libcef/common/resource_util.cc
+++ b/libcef/common/resource_util.cc
@@ -126,6 +126,12 @@ base::FilePath GetUserDataPath(CefSettings* settings,
 // to the desktop on any platform.
 // From chrome/browser/download/download_prefs.cc.
 bool DownloadPathIsDangerous(const base::FilePath& download_path) {
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_AROS)
+  // The AROS provider deliberately uses RAM: for downloads. It has no POSIX
+  // home/desktop relationship to classify, and querying DIR_USER_DESKTOP
+  // attempts to canonicalize "." through stat(), which is not an AROS path.
+  return false;
+#else
 #if BUILDFLAG(IS_LINUX)
   base::FilePath home_dir = base::GetHomeDir();
   if (download_path == home_dir) {
@@ -139,6 +145,7 @@ bool DownloadPathIsDangerous(const base::FilePath& download_path) {
     return false;
   }
   return (download_path == desktop_dir);
+#endif
 }
 
 bool GetDefaultDownloadDirectory(base::FilePath* result) {
